# F45 resource-dependent identity context

The new `syson_domain::identity_context` module implements the pinned ElementUtil UUID branch decisions over explicit immutable observations, reusing the existing UUIDv5 implementation. It supplies no random generator or native EMF/resource/getter adapter. Every call consumes exactly one caller-supplied v4 UUID before checking the context, including deterministic branches and null-element failure, preserving the eager upstream call. Provider failure, invalid v4 output and exhaustion are explicit; no retry or substitute provider is selected.

A standard LibraryPackage with an available resource/URI and qualified name hashes the URL namespace plus KerML/SysML base and raw name. Only the exact `kermllibrary:` prefix selects KerML; all other URI strings select SysML, including ordinary URIs. Absent resource or null qualified name keeps the fresh UUID; a reached null URI is a distinct failure. Nonroot elements use the standard library namespace ID only when declared name is nonnull, the class is not Import/Membership/Specialization/TypeFeaturing, and qualified name is nonnull. Empty names count as present. Source caller class predicates include subtypes; this module does not infer them.

Absent versus unresolved observations remain distinct, and branch-unreached values are not resolved. The observation record represents stable getter facts; changing getter results, native namespace lookup, EMF notifications/proxies and external resource loading remain unimplemented. Null/error outcomes are typed Rust outcomes rather than Java exception objects. Namespace UUID parsing accepts fixed-width canonical-shaped text with either hex case; additional Java UUID.fromString forms remain explicitly unsupported.

`SemanticId` and `ResourceId` retain separate roles. Selected field admission preserves the original supplied text, allows equal values across roles and rejects same-role duplicates by UUID value. The document-local reservation registry checks both roles before mutation. This collision policy is a proposed selected-adapter facility, not a claim that upstream UUID generation performs collision checks. Separate registry instances are separate scopes. Full SysONIdentityService default identity/IDAdapter behavior remains outside this module.

Eighteen source-derived domain tests cover every selected generation branch, eager provider use/exhaustion, lazy errors, source UUID goldens, exact Unicode name hashing and atomic collision admission. The standalone integration harness uses only existing domain/model/workflow path dependencies. It imports the actual 11-object selected EMF JSON fixture, creates a package with generated semantic and explicit separate resource identity, cancels edits, rejects semantic/resource collisions, and saves/reloads real immutable SnapshotStore files through a fresh handle. This is actual local selected-adapter integration, not full native EMF interchange or crash recovery. It requires an existing absolute SYSON_TEST_DIR canonicalized under /workspace; only its own new test subdirectory is written and retained.

SOURCE-CONTRACT.json records pinned sources, input restrictions and exact helper boundaries. The first copied harness lock was refused by Cargo --locked before integration test execution; it was not a product assertion failure. The coordinator preserved that original lock and regenerated only the new harness lock offline. Registry package records, versions, sources and checksums remain unchanged. Actual resolution pruned the inactive local syson-initializer and syson-initializer-graph records and removed optional graph/metamodel edges from the syson-workflow row, leaving syson-editor, syson-model and syson-persistence; the harness itself is the sole new local package. `reproduce.py` now checks exactly this inspected graph, rather than assuming an unchanged copy was valid. Coordinator f45-domain-01 passed all 18 new tests plus 28 existing domain/query regressions; f45-integration-02 passed the actual file-backed integration test. Both suites passed formatting and Clippy with warnings denied. [The validation record](../../follow-ons/F45/VALIDATION.json) links original failure/passing receipts and [the distinct source review](../../follow-ons/F45/REVIEW.md). The coordinator also executed the captures; no second runtime executor is claimed. All passing-capture input hashes remain unchanged. The worker has not executed Cargo, Java or an oracle, and upstream runtime comparison remains NOT_RUN.
